x86: add the /dev/harmony synchronous SDK transport

Applications and agents must not need iopl(2) or /dev/mem to reach Harmony's
deterministic doorbell. Add a built-in misc character device which owns the
fixed request and response pages, serializes every exchange, emits attributed
Antithesis JSON on write(2), implements deterministic entropy as a one-byte
write followed by an eight-byte read, carries the SDK coverage-threshold command
as a 17-byte write followed by a 12-byte read, and exposes a bounded raw-frame
ioctl for guest agents. The hypercall remains the existing OUT 0x0ca1 path. A
KUnit concurrency test blocks one in-flight transaction and proves a second
ringer cannot enter the page/doorbell critical section.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository's kernel-patch exception.

---
--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -647,6 +647,29 @@
 source "drivers/misc/c2port/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/eeprom/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/cb710/Kconfig"
+
+config HARMONY_DEVICE
+	bool "Harmony deterministic hypercall character device"
+	depends on X86_64
+	default n
+	help
+	  Expose /dev/harmony for synchronous application traffic to the
+	  Harmony deterministic hypervisor. Writes emit Antithesis-compatible
+	  JSON with caller attribution; a one-byte NUL write followed by an
+	  eight-byte read obtains entropy from the seeded hypercall stream.
+	  The driver owns the fixed 0xe000/0xf000 frame pages and rings I/O
+	  port 0x0ca1, so applications need neither /dev/mem nor iopl(2).
+
+config HARMONY_DEVICE_KUNIT_TEST
+	bool "KUnit test for Harmony transaction serialization"
+	depends on HARMONY_DEVICE && KUNIT
+	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
+	help
+	  Drive two concurrent callers against an intentionally blocked Harmony
+	  transaction and prove that only one caller can enter the fixed-page
+	  exchange at a time. This catches removal or narrowing of the driver
+	  mutex which owns the request page, doorbell, and response page.
+
 source "drivers/misc/lis3lv02d/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/altera-stapl/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/mei/Kconfig"
